WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.579
In the previous video, you saw us renewing an&nbsp;old pickup truck.

00:00:06.327 --> 00:00:11.760
And in this video, we're going to upgrade
 an old shipping container for future&nbsp;storage and materials.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.546
We will start by making a big roof above it, 
and we're going to share all&nbsp;the drawings with you...

00:00:16.546 --> 00:00:19.166
So you can use it for your own container, 
if you have one laying around...

00:00:19.481 --> 00:00:22.427
But, first things first: we need a shipping container...

00:00:22.427 --> 00:00:26.051
And we got one a few months ago,
in the middle&nbsp;of a rainy winter...

00:00:26.481 --> 00:00:27.157
Our land?

00:00:27.157 --> 00:00:28.945
It's a bit rough with the dirt roads...

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:32.830
So we had to move it to&nbsp;a more sketchy truck,
to bring it to the land.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.280
 

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.240
 

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.360
 

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.280
 

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.080
 

00:01:02.822 --> 00:01:04.408
We are now in the back of Basekamp!

00:01:04.408 --> 00:01:06.322
We&nbsp;cleared all these mimosa patches...

00:01:06.752 --> 00:01:09.286
We cleared all this area, where the container&nbsp;is going to come...

00:01:09.286 --> 00:01:16.072
Then, we have put these concrete pieces, 
to let the container rest flat&nbsp;on top.

00:01:16.072 --> 00:01:19.223
Now that it's raining, the container needs to come by the path...

00:01:19.223 --> 00:01:21.346
We also cleared the path for the&nbsp;truck.

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:23.340
Let's see how it goes...

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.996
Coming in five minutes!

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.560
 

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.760
 

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.040
 

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.480
 

00:01:53.999 --> 00:01:54.499
 

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.210
Looks good...

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:31.710
huh

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:32.560
looks good!

00:02:32.702 --> 00:02:34.520
 

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.640
 

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.800
 

00:02:39.161 --> 00:02:41.080
 

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:50.977
Good!

00:02:50.977 --> 00:02:53.880
I'm impacted with this&nbsp;rain, but the driver is badass.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.660
Happy, for a new dry space!

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.255
So here we have the container!

00:03:10.255 --> 00:03:11.335
It's currently&nbsp;spring...

00:03:11.335 --> 00:03:13.461
It's been here since the winter.

00:03:13.461 --> 00:03:17.072
We put some stuff inside, to make sure it 
was protected from&nbsp;the rain.

00:03:17.072 --> 00:03:22.818
But now, the sun is coming, 
and it's time to rebuild this beautiful container.

00:03:23.277 --> 00:03:28.302
So when we&nbsp;got the container we made a patch 
free from vegetation, where we could put it.

00:03:28.302 --> 00:03:32.408
But everything&nbsp;around it is still very dense and overgrown..

00:03:32.408 --> 00:03:35.191
With some mimosa trees, some old branches that are&nbsp;there...

00:03:35.191 --> 00:03:38.646
So we still need to clean up the area 
around it a bit, so we have space.

00:03:38.646 --> 00:03:42.545
But also for the&nbsp;fire season that is coming,
to make sure we remove the 'fuel'...

00:03:42.545 --> 00:03:45.332
And we're gonna make a big roof on top&nbsp;of the container.

00:03:45.647 --> 00:03:47.961
It's going to be the biggest roof we have until now!

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:52.116
And we mainly want this, because&nbsp;we want 
to store things very dry in the container.

00:03:52.116 --> 00:03:58.339
But also, create some dry spaces on the edges of&nbsp;it,
so we can store wood, metal, our waste system...

00:03:58.712 --> 00:04:02.778
The roof itself will be mounted on these four,
solid corners, which containers always have.

00:04:02.778 --> 00:04:04.581
Wait, let me actually show you up close...

00:04:04.581 --> 00:04:08.619
They look a bit rough, but&nbsp;they're super sturdy
and standardized around the world.

00:04:08.619 --> 00:04:11.534
So the drying would be replicable to other&nbsp;containers.

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:15.335
And, for us, it also means in the future
that we can take it on and off, if we want to.

00:04:15.335 --> 00:04:17.253
Because it's a very solid connection.

00:04:17.253 --> 00:04:20.321
And the outside of the container is in pretty rough condition...

00:04:20.321 --> 00:04:21.271
Very&nbsp;rusty...

00:04:21.271 --> 00:04:25.867
But I think we'll just leave it like that,
because we're going to have a big roof on top, that&nbsp;will protect it...

00:04:26.211 --> 00:04:29.456
And these containers are also very resistant against all the rust.

00:04:29.456 --> 00:04:30.787
So it should be&nbsp;okay...

00:04:30.787 --> 00:04:34.058
But the inside we're gonna make very nice and clean.

00:04:34.058 --> 00:04:36.277
Organized with tools and bulk storage.

00:04:36.277 --> 00:04:38.135
But before we're going to do any of that...

00:04:38.135 --> 00:04:40.203
- We will need to clear a bit more around it.

00:04:41.407 --> 00:04:43.644
We need to make some&nbsp;space around the container.

00:04:43.644 --> 00:04:48.063
And in case you don't know, our land is fully 
overgrown with invasive&nbsp;tree species...

00:04:48.063 --> 00:04:52.536
This, in combination with having the summer 
around the corner, means wildfires are&nbsp;coming.

00:04:52.536 --> 00:04:55.020
A big reason to take flammable mimosas down!

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:18.473
Okay, one patch down!

00:05:18.473 --> 00:05:19.703
Another&nbsp;one to come!

00:05:22.082 --> 00:05:23.520
With the new gloves...

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.183
Not in shape yet...

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:34.121
It's the beginning of the season...

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.796
It's catching fire...

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:31.560
After we chopped all&nbsp;the mimosas, we burned all the brambles,
and the things that could spread a fire.

00:06:54.402 --> 00:06:57.685
And, as we have a lot of logs now, we offer them to the neighbors

00:06:57.685 --> 00:07:00.060
Who use them for&nbsp;warming up their house in the winter.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:30.484
And we also had help from Benjamin, 
to&nbsp;turn the leftovers into wood chips.

00:07:30.484 --> 00:07:34.200
That will prevent that more mimosas,
and&nbsp;brambles would grow in the new area.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.760
- Did we finish, Julie?
- Yes.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.360
Enough.

00:08:41.116 --> 00:08:43.765
Alright! So, this is a much better pile!

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:47.102
Now we have a lot of wood chips to be spread...

00:08:58.393 --> 00:09:02.293
Now that this area is clean,
Dave can&nbsp;start to build the new storage room.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:07.215
Now it's a new day.

00:09:07.215 --> 00:09:11.040
All the materials for the roof structure arrived,
so we&nbsp;can start building the frame.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.880
 

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.520
 

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:35.464
So next, we're gonna make the frame on top of&nbsp;the roof.

00:09:35.464 --> 00:09:42.380
And make sure we have a way to connect it, 
using one long beam on top, with a few nuts&nbsp;and bolts...

00:09:43.345 --> 00:09:45.965
So let's see if we can make it fit!

00:10:02.097 --> 00:10:06.300
The roof itself is pretty irregular and&nbsp;not straight,
because there's a lot of bumps...

00:10:07.184 --> 00:10:11.336
We want to make sure that it's all flat
before we start building the roof...

00:10:11.336 --> 00:10:16.721
So we can put two big beams on both sides
to even&nbsp;out everything.

00:10:16.721 --> 00:10:22.200
On those are also going to be the connector points 
where the roof&nbsp;is going to be attached to the container.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.506
Next we're going to make the metal frame.

00:11:01.509 --> 00:11:04.143
We need to chop all the metal tubing we have and strips.

00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:08.582
So cutting, drilling, and&nbsp;then welding it together.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:36.340
So we have these 6-meter-long beams 
and they&nbsp;go all the way back to the container...

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:37.892
But they don't fully fit in.

00:12:37.892 --> 00:12:40.209
So if you have to drill&nbsp;a hole in the middle...

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.101
Uh, yeah, it doesn't fit...

00:12:42.615 --> 00:12:48.119
But in order to make it fit, we could&nbsp;make a hole in the container,
so the beam can slide all the way through.

00:12:49.825 --> 00:12:52.054
Just need to make a little hole in the container...

00:12:52.054 --> 00:12:55.385
And then we can continue&nbsp;to drill all of the holes.

00:12:55.614 --> 00:12:58.043
Right there...

00:14:01.148 --> 00:14:02.294
- You are not filming?

00:14:02.294 --> 00:14:03.119
No, I just started now...

00:14:03.119 --> 00:14:04.679
- Ah okay, no, keep going...

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:51.127
All right, so all the metal parts are now cut!

00:14:51.356 --> 00:14:54.096
All the brackets&nbsp;and the tubes and next 
we're going to weld it.

00:14:54.096 --> 00:14:59.220
Now we're going to weld&nbsp;it into a few parts,
that we later can assemble on top of the&nbsp;container.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.754
So now it's time to weld!

00:15:44.228 --> 00:15:46.911
All the holders are now welded and secured.

00:15:46.911 --> 00:15:51.980
This is the only&nbsp;welding we have to do, 
because all the rest will be nuts and bolts, holding it together.

00:15:52.704 --> 00:15:55.330
Next step: we're going to give this a paint job,
 to make sure they're protected.

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:58.480
And then we're&nbsp;gonna assemble everything on the container!

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:36.298
Show your hands!

00:16:37.215 --> 00:16:41.503
- Now it's a bit clean, because I cleaned them a bit...

00:16:41.704 --> 00:16:42.727
Now they're clean?

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.088
- Yeah that's clean. I swear!

00:16:51.173 --> 00:16:52.214
Okay!

00:16:53.093 --> 00:16:55.204
Sanding and cleaning: done!

00:16:55.204 --> 00:16:56.640
Next up: painting.

00:17:38.665 --> 00:17:40.046
Okay, so all the parts are now ready!

00:17:40.046 --> 00:17:42.656
We&nbsp;have the screws, the bolts, the nuts, and wrenches...

00:17:42.656 --> 00:17:45.036
Container is here, so today we're going to put it&nbsp;all together!

00:17:45.036 --> 00:17:46.628
We have Jaime here to help out!

00:17:47.029 --> 00:17:48.905
- Hello, my name is Jaime!

00:17:49.679 --> 00:17:51.550
I'm 29 years old, and&nbsp;I'm from Spain.

00:17:52.009 --> 00:17:54.214
I've been traveling in my van for the last few years.

00:17:54.214 --> 00:17:57.844
Working and developing&nbsp;my skills as a carpenter
in different parts of Europe.

00:17:58.417 --> 00:18:02.934
I came to Project Kamp to experience&nbsp;
a more self-sustaining, self-sufficient mode of living...

00:18:02.934 --> 00:18:05.263
In a community and in a natural&nbsp;environment.

00:18:05.263 --> 00:18:08.504
I like to travel, get to know new places, cultures...

00:18:08.504 --> 00:18:12.869
And, in the future, I&nbsp;would like to buy 
a piece of land with a ruin to rebuild it....

00:18:12.869 --> 00:18:15.624
And life a lifestyle that is&nbsp;more environment-friendly.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.828
So let's start working!

00:19:15.542 --> 00:19:18.863
So, next, we're gonna connect the frame to&nbsp;the container.

00:19:19.236 --> 00:19:22.376
So we made these brackets that we put underneath...

00:19:22.376 --> 00:19:25.650
And then we can bolt them together...

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.800
So they clamp themselves to&nbsp;the container, 
and it should be solid.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.312
So next is the last layer on the frame.

00:20:23.973 --> 00:20:25.504
It's&nbsp;two different tubes...

00:20:25.504 --> 00:20:29.750
So in order to bring them together, 
we have this little piece of wood that&nbsp;goes into the tube...

00:20:30.208 --> 00:20:31.518
And we hammer it in there.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.246
And then the other one as&nbsp;well

00:20:35.647 --> 00:20:39.461
Then, we make sure they're all aligned, 
and we screw them onto the frame.

00:21:07.301 --> 00:21:08.502
- It's dirty...

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:11.458
So the&nbsp;roof is now ready with the frame! 

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:13.447
It's pretty smooth!

00:21:13.447 --> 00:21:15.646
And next, we're gonna put on&nbsp;the roof.

00:21:16.534 --> 00:21:18.928
Next, we need to get the materials for the roof

00:21:18.928 --> 00:21:22.886
We picked them up on our brand new&nbsp;pickup, 
which we renovated in previous video.

00:21:23.115 --> 00:21:27.424
It's great to have a bigger sturdy car,
to be&nbsp;able to get larger things ourselves.

00:21:27.654 --> 00:21:32.171
And, for the roofing material, we went for metal sheets, 
which&nbsp;is very commonly used around here...

00:21:32.572 --> 00:21:36.354
You can find more information in the research module,
 on why&nbsp;we're using this material.

00:21:36.669 --> 00:21:39.231
And there you can also download all the files to build the frame.

00:21:39.489 --> 00:21:40.913
The link&nbsp;is posted below!

00:21:41.458 --> 00:21:45.077
For now: time to put on the roof.

00:21:51.420 --> 00:21:52.960
So the first panel is on...

00:21:54.078 --> 00:21:55.596
What are we going to do now?

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.120
- I'm gonna drill the first hole...

00:21:59.496 --> 00:22:01.450
And we already&nbsp;created some shade!

00:22:01.794 --> 00:22:02.294
- A bit.

00:22:02.466 --> 00:22:04.402
There -- a rectangular shade.

00:22:05.291 --> 00:22:07.594
- I think shade is going to come, when the&nbsp;roof is up...

00:22:07.594 --> 00:22:10.042
It's gonna be a hot evening!

00:23:07.480 --> 00:23:09.909
I'm currently on the roof, and everything is finished

00:23:09.909 --> 00:23:12.106
But, I kind of cannot get off...

00:23:12.708 --> 00:23:18.514
The plan is to jump in that pile of wood chips,
and hopefully everything is okay...

00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:36.233
The assembling of the roof went surprisingly&nbsp;smooth!

00:23:36.233 --> 00:23:40.113
All the pieces fitted without a problem, 
and we assembled everything in&nbsp;one day!

00:23:40.729 --> 00:23:45.783
But just as you finish the roof and wanted to get a dinner, 
a guy showed up with his big digger...

00:23:52.140 --> 00:23:56.453
He should come on Saturday, but he just came today,
 because he is going&nbsp;to flatten the area around it.

00:23:56.453 --> 00:24:00.000
Which is going to be nice in the future, 
because then it's&nbsp;all flattened.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:03.716
And he also will take out the roots, 
that we didn't manage to do&nbsp;ourselves before...

00:24:04.404 --> 00:24:05.278
So, yeah...

00:24:06.080 --> 00:24:07.731
Final touches!

00:24:59.880 --> 00:25:00.984
Alright, so...

00:25:00.984 --> 00:25:02.022
The roof is now ready!

00:25:02.022 --> 00:25:04.970
We already tested it yesterday,&nbsp;with some rain coming in...

00:25:09.840 --> 00:25:12.233
Perfectly dry underneath, so that's good.

00:25:12.634 --> 00:25:19.772
The&nbsp;next steps are going to be making space on the back side,
to store material like wood and metal, that we have leftover.

00:25:19.772 --> 00:25:23.266
And, on this side, it's going to be a waste system, 
where we can sort out all our trash.

00:25:23.639 --> 00:25:26.644
On the inside, we're going to store the garden&nbsp;tools and bulk food.

00:25:27.189 --> 00:25:28.785
But, that's for later videos...

00:25:28.785 --> 00:25:30.686
If you want to see those, make sure&nbsp;to subscribe.

00:25:30.915 --> 00:25:33.910
So you're going to continue to follow how this is going to go.

00:25:33.910 --> 00:25:39.400
And if you already&nbsp;want to see the next video for next week, 
make sure to subscribe and support on Patreon.

00:25:39.400 --> 00:25:41.072
So you can see it one week ahead!

00:25:41.072 --> 00:25:42.626
But if not, no worries...

00:25:42.626 --> 00:25:45.228
You are going to see us same time, same channel, next week!

00:25:45.744 --> 00:25:47.016
Thanks for watching!

00:25:52.260 --> 00:25:53.040
It's very strong!

00:26:00.542 --> 00:26:01.271
That was it.

00:26:01.271 --> 00:26:01.771
Thanks for watching.

